  "name": "Question 9",
  "problem": "Solve the inequality $5x\\cdot {7}^{2x+3}+4\\cdot {7}^{2x+3}\\ge -2\\cdot {7}^{2x+3}.$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we move all the terms to the left side of the inequality and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x\\cdot {7}^{2x+3}+4\\cdot {7}^{2x+3} & \\ge -2\\cdot {7}^{2x+3} \\\\ 5x\\cdot {7}^{2x+3}+4\\cdot {7}^{2x+3}+2\\cdot {7}^{2x+3} & \\ge 0 \\\\ (5x+4+2){7}^{2x+3} & \\ge 0 \\\\ (5x+6){7}^{2x+3} & \\ge 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both sides by ${7}^{2x+3}$ and solve the resulting inequality using familiar techniques:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x+6 & \\ge 0 \\\\ 5x & \\ge -6 \\\\ x & \\ge -\\frac{6}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to the inequality above is $x\\ge -\\frac{6}{5}.$",
